yphen line. The length of line 9 is 46, including the two spaces. So why is the error 96? That doesn\'t make sense. Perhaps the error is on a different line.\n\nWait, looking back, the error messages are:\n\n5:13: truthy value should be one of [false, true] (truthy)\n9:81: line too long (92 > 80 characters) (line-length)\n23:81: line too long (96 > 80 characters) (line-length)\n\nSo line 5 is the first task, line 9 is the \'when\' line, and line 23 is the \'raw\' module line.\n\nWait, perhaps the line numbers are off because the playbook starts with --- and has lines before the tasks. Let me count the lines in the original playbook.\n\nThe original playbook is:\n\n---\n- name: Check if all variables have been set correctly\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  delegate_to: localhost\n  run_once: yes\n\n- name: Wait for host to be reachable\n  wait_for:\n    host: "{{ ansible_ssh_host | default(\'ansible_host\') | default(\'inventory_hostname\') }}"\n    port: 22\n    state: started\n    timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout | default(\'300\') }}"\n  become: true\n  become_user: "{{ bootstrap_user | default(\'ansible_user\') }}"\n  when:\n    - ansible_connection not in ["container", "docker"]\n    - bootstrap_wait_for_host | default(true) | bool\n\n- name: Prepare the system\n  block:\n    - name: Test connection\n      wait_for_connection:\n        host: "{{ ansible_ssh_host | default(\'ansible_host\') | default(\'inventory_hostname\') }}"\n        port: 22\n        timeout: "{{ bootstrap_timeout | default(\'300\') }}"\n        register: bootstrap_connect\n        until: "\'ansible connect success\' in bootstrap_connect.msg"\n        retries: 3\n        delay: 10\n\n    - name: Gather bootstrap facts\n      import_tasks: gather_facts.yml\n\n- name: Install bootstrap packages\n  raw:\n    cmd: "{{ bootstrap_packages_cmd }}"\n  register: bootstrap_install_packages\n  user: "{{ bootstrap_user | default(\'ansible_user\') }}"\n  become: true\n  become_user: "{{ bootstrap_user | default(\'ansible_user\') }}"\n\n- name: Ensure system is prepared by issuing ansible modules\n  block:\n    - name: Gather ansible facts\n      setup:\n        gather_subset: \'!passwords\'\n\n    - name: Install packages listed in bootstrap__facts_packages\n      package:\n        name: "{{ bootstrap__facts_packages | default([]) | list }}"\n        state: present\n\nSo line 5 is the end of the first task. Line 6 is the start of the second task. Line 9 is the \'when\' line.\n\nWait, line 5 is the last line of the first task, so line 5 is "run_once: yes".\n\nThen line 6 is the start of the second task: "- name: Wait for host to be reachable".\n\nLines 7-11 are the \'wait_for\' module.\n\nLine 12 is \'become: true\'.\n\nLine 13 is \'become_user: ...\'.\n\nLine 14 is \'when:\'.\n\nLines 15-16 are the \'when\' conditions.\n\nSo the error on line 5:13 is on the \'run_once: yes\' line, which is line 5, column 13. The value is \'yes\', which is a string, but \'run_once\' expects a boolean. So perhaps the issue is that \'yes\' is a truthy value, but it\'s not a boolean. In YAML, \'yes\' is allowed as a boolean, but perhaps yamllint expects it to be \'true\' or \'false\'.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the issue is that \'run_once\' is a keyword that expects a boolean, and \'yes\' is not a boolean in YAML. Wait, in YAML, \'yes\' is a valid boolean equivalent, but perhaps the linter is strict and expects \'true\' or \'false\'.\n\nSo to fix the first error, I should change \'yes\' to \'true\' in the \'run_once\' parameter.\n\nSo, the first task\'s \'run_once\' line should be:\n\nrun_once: true\n\nInstead of \'yes\'.\n\nThat would fix the truthy value issue.\n\nNow, for the line length errors.\n\nLine 9:81 is the \'when\' line, which is line 15 in the original playbook. The line is:\n\n- ansible_connection not in ["container", "docker"]\n\nWhich is 44 characters, including the two spaces. But the error says 92 > 80. So perhaps the line is longer than that.\n\nWait, perhaps the line is:\n\nansible_connection not in ["container", "docker"]\n\nWhich is 40 characters, but with the indentation, it\'s 44. So why is the line length 92? Maybe I\'m misunderstanding the line numbers.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the line is:\n\nwhen:\n  - ansible_connection not in ["container", "docker"]\n\nWhich is line 14 and 15. The line in question is line 15, which is 44 characters, under 80.\n\nBut the error says line 9:81, which suggests line 9, column 81. So perhaps the line is longer than 80.\n\nWait, perhaps the line is:\n\nansible_connection not in ["container", "docker"]\n\nWhich is 40 characters, but with the indentation, it\'s 44, which is under 80.\n\nSo perhaps the error is on line 23, which is the \'raw\' module line.\n\nLooking at the original playbook, line 23 is:\n\nuser: "{{ bootstrap_user | default(\'ansible_user\') }}"\n\nWhich is 51 characters, under 80.\n\nWait, perhaps the error is on the \'when\' line, which is line 15, but the line is not too long. So perhaps the issue is elsewhere.\n\nWait, perhaps the error is on the \'when\' line because it\'s using a list, and yamllint is expecting a single boolean. But in Ansible, \'when\' can take a list, so that\'s correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps the issue is that the \'when\' clause is using a list, and yamllint is expecting a single value, hence the truthy error.\n\nWait, perhaps the first error is due to the \'run_once\' parameter using \'yes\' instead of \'true\'.\n\nSo, to fix the first error, change \'run_once: yes\' to \'run_once: true\'.\n\nFor the line length errors, perhaps the lines are within 80, but the linter is being strict. Alternatively, perhaps the lines are indeed too long, and I need to split them.\n\nFor the \'when\' line, I can split it into multiple lines, each under 80 characters.\n\nFor example:\n\nwhen:\n  - ansible_connection not in\n    ["container", "docker"]\n  - bootstrap_wait_for_host | default(\n      true) | bool\n\nThis way, each line is within 80 characters.\n\nSimilarl