content='<think>\nAlright, I need to generate an Ansible Playbook based on the given tasks. Let me start by understanding the requirements. The playbook must be valid for an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory, so it should only contain tasks without any playbook-level directives.\n\nFirst, Task 1 is to import assert.yml, but only on localhost. I remember that in Ansible, importing tasks is done with the import_tasks module. So I\'ll set the file to assert.yml and specify the host as localhost.\n\nNext, Tasks 2 to 7 involve configuring different package managers. Each task needs to check if the system uses a specific package manager. I\'ll use the apt, apk, dnf, yum, pacman, and zypper modules accordingly. For each, I\'ll add conditions to only run when the package manager is detected. For example, using apt when ansible_pkg_manager == \'apt\'.\n\nFor Tasks 2 and 3, I need to update the cache and upgrade, but with some conditions. Task 2 uses apk, so I\'ll call apk update and upgrade. Task 3 uses apt, so I\'ll update the cache with apt update and upgrade using apt with the upgrade flag. Also, I need to exclude certain packages defined in update_excluded_packages. I\'ll use the loop parameter with exclude_packages.\n\nTasks 4, 5, and 6 involve dnf, pacman, and yum respectively. For dnf, I\'ll check if the package manager is dnf or dnf5. I\'ll use dnf module with the update flag and exclude the specified packages. For pacman, I\'ll use pacman with the sync flag. Yum is a bit trickier because it behaves differently in version 6, so I\'ll use the yum module with the version check and handle the state accordingly.\n\nEach task that upgrades packages notifies the Reboot handler after completion. I\'ll make sure to include the notify keyword in these tasks pointing to the Reboot handler.\n\nI need to structure each task properly, ensuring the correct module names and parameters. I\'ll also ensure that the tasks are in the order specified and that each has the necessary conditions to only run when applicable.\n\nFinally, I\'ll format everything in YAML, starting with \'---\' and ensuring that each task is correctly indented and follows YAML syntax. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations, keeping the playbook clean and only containing the tasks as specified.\n</think>\n\n```\n---\n- name: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks:\n    file: assert.yml\n  args:\n    host: localhost\n\n- name: Configure apk\n  apk:\n    update_cache: yes\n    upgrade: yes\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'apk\'\n\n- name: Configure apt\n  apt:\n    cache_valid_time: 3600\n    update_cache: yes\n    upgrade: yes\n    exclude_packages: "{{ update_excluded_packages | default([]) | list }}"\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'apt\'\n\n- name: Update all software (dnf)\n  dnf:\n    update: yes\n    exclude: "{{ update_excluded_packages | default([]) | list }}"\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr in [\'dnf\', \'dnf5\']\n\n- name: Update all software (pacman)\n  pacman:\n    sync: yes\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'pacman\'\n\n- name: Configure yum\n  yum:\n    name: "{{ item }}"\n    state: present\n  loop: "{{ update_excluded_packages | default([]) | list }}"\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'yum\' and ansible_yum_version != \'6\'\n\n- name: Update all software (zypper)\n  zypper:\n    update: yes\n  notify: Reboot\n  when: ansible_pkg_mgr == \'zypper\'\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T21:53:40.400380931Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12345635665, 'load_duration': 85447015, 'prompt_eval_count': 597, 'prompt_eval_duration': 258321278, 'eval_count': 810, 'eval_duration': 12000250589, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--0260dc30-31af-4333-b444-e14af8520789-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 597, 'output_tokens': 810, 'total_tokens': 1407}
