 in both tasks.\n\nNow, putting it all together, I\'ll start the playbook with \'---\', then list the tasks in the specified order. I\'ll make sure the YAML syntax is correct, avoiding any comments or extra lines. Each task should be a YAML block under the main playbook structure.\n\nI should double-check the module names and parameters to ensure accuracy. For the first task, the module is `community.general.apache2_module`, and for the second, it\'s `template`. Also, the handler notifications must match the names provided.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure that the playbook doesn\'t include any unnecessary elements, only the tasks as specified. That should meet all the user\'s requirements.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Enable Apache modules\n  community.general.apache2_module:\n    name: [\'proxy\', \'proxy_http\']\n    state: present\n  become: yes\n  become_method: sudo\n\n- name: Configure Apache locations\n  template:\n    src: location.conf.j2\n    dest: "{{ httpd_config_directory }}/{{ item.name }}"\n    permissions: 0644\n  loop: "{{ httpd_locations }}"\n  become: yes\n  become_method: sudo\n  notify: \n    - Test httpd configuration validity\n    - Restart httpd\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-20T23:01:40.194832338Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 10943608567, 'load_duration': 102009188, 'prompt_eval_count': 400, 'prompt_eval_duration': 93096658, 'eval_count': 726, 'eval_duration': 10747598278, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--a220afa3-65c9-4e53-8cce-f15f0aad8e27-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 400, 'output_tokens': 726, 'total_tokens': 1126}
